\"\"\"              onChanged: (v) {\n                setState(() => _terms = v ?? false);\n                if (_terms) Analytics.capture('terms_accepted');\n              },\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"                  ? () => Navigator.of(context).pushNamed('/offers')\"\"\",\"\"\"                  ? () {\n                      Analytics.capture('registration_continue_tapped', {\n                        'amount': _amount.round(),\n                        'terms': _terms,\n                      });\n                      Navigator.of(context).pushNamed('/offers');\n                    }\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='lib/screens/offer_screen.dart'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\\n\",\"import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\\n\\nimport '../analytics.dart';\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"      body: ListView.builder(\",\"\"\"      body: NotificationListener<ScrollEndNotification>(\n        // Once per finished scroll, not per scroll update.\n        onNotification: (n) {\n          Analytics.capture('offers_scrolled', {'offset': n.metrics.pixels});\n          return false;\n        },\n        child: ListView.builder(\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"        },\n      ),\n    );\"\"\",\"\"\"        },\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Analytics events implementation\n\nAll six events from docs/EVENTS.md are implemented through `Analytics.capture`, with names and properties unchanged.\n\n- `registration_email_started` and `registration_phone_started` fire from `onChanged` on the first edit only. A `_emailStartedFired` or `_phoneStartedFired` flag on the screen state stops repeats. No email or phone value is sent.\n- `loan_amount_changed` (`amount` as an int) fires from the slider's `onChangeEnd`, so once per drag. `onChanged` only updates the UI.\n- `terms_accepted` fires when the checkbox changes to ticked. Unticking sends nothing.\n- `registration_continue_tapped` (`amount`, `terms`) fires on the Continue tap, before navigation.\n- `offers_scrolled` (`offset` as `metrics.pixels`) fires from a `NotificationListener<ScrollEndNotification>`, so once per finished scroll rather than per scroll update.\n\n## Colleague's note\n- **Applied:** the once-per-visit flags for the text fields, `onChangeEnd` for the slider and `ScrollEndNotification` for scrolling. The spec's wording (\"started typing\", \"moved the slider\", \"scrolled\") would otherwise have led to per-keystroke and per-step events and a quickly exhausted quota.\n- **Not applicable:** focus-lost capture, because no event needs a field's final value. I made no changes to the PostHog config or debug settings.\n\n## Not verified\nI didn't build or run the app, and I didn't run `flutter analyze`.\n\nThe flags are per screen-state instance. If the screen is rebuilt, they reset.\nE\ngit diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1690,"cache_read_input_tokens":22816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1690},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4f32edb-19b1-41db-aba2-620b8542e0e9","uuid":"c1e8c9ad-aa7a-4256-af38-2b19376d15b2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:27:33.753Z","request_id":"req_011CgS2j5vtyqcPB7G6WRTJa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Mq3jemXJUysAbLZUJRS1kY":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-9kTyBW && python3 - <<'E'\np='lib/screens/registration_screen.dart'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\\n\",\"import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\\n\\nimport '../analytics.dart';\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"  bool _terms = false;\\n\",\"  bool _terms = false;\\n  bool _emailStartedFired = false;\\n  bool _phoneStartedFired = false;\\n\",1)\ns=s.re