{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2jyvkvTj8xHK2wjHJJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens, using `Analytics.capture`. Event names and properties match the spec. I didn't build or run the app, and I didn't run `flutter analyze`.\n\nThe spec's wording would have meant an event per keystroke and per slider step, so I fired each event once per interaction:\n\n- **Email and phone started:** fires on the first edit only, using a flag on the screen state. No email or phone value is sent.\n- **Loan amount changed:** fires from the slider's `onChangeEnd`, so once per drag, with `amount` as an int.\n- **Terms accepted:** fires when the checkbox is ticked. Unticking sends nothing.\n- **Continue tapped:** fires on the tap, with `amount` and `terms`.\n- **Offers scrolled:** fires from a `ScrollEndNotification` listener, so once per finished scroll, with `offset` as the scroll position.\n\nThe flags are per screen-state instance, so they reset if the screen is rebuilt.\n\n`ANSWER.md` records what I did and which parts of your colleague's note applied. The once-per-visit flags, `onChangeEnd` for the slider and `ScrollEndNotification` for scrolling applied. Their focus-lost approach didn't, because no event needs a field's final value."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1995,"cache_read_input_tokens":24506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1995},"output_tokens":434,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4f32edb-19b1-41db-aba2-620b8542e0e9","uuid":"9fef8b86-2b97-45f5-ac09-d221fef2b1e8","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:27:37.335Z","request_id":"req_0